# WRONG: equiv coerces the second function's result to the first function's
# result type before comparing, so a narrowing cast looks like an identity.
# f(-128) = 128 (u8), g(-128) = -128 (i32), yet equiv says "equal ... exhaustive".
f(x: i8) = u8(x)
g(x: i8) = i32(x)
show f(-128)
show g(-128)
show f(-1)
show g(-1)
equiv f g
